PR #365 (Mathjk) - APPLIED as eed7415 (cherry-pick, author kept, message references the PR).
- Read: 2 functions in path.rs (Windows only) + Windows-only test. Replaces to_str().unwrap()
  with as_encoded_bytes()/from_encoded_bytes_unchecked(). Flagged spot: the `unsafe`
  from_encoded_bytes_unchecked. Checked every way a Path component is built (os_to_c_str from
  an OsStr, CString literals ".", components copied from existing Paths, stfu8-decoded strings
  converted via OsString) - all are valid OsStr encodings, so the SAFETY comment holds.
  Remaining `CString::new(..).unwrap()` on interior NUL is unchanged and the same as on Unix.
- Verified: cross-check for x86_64-pc-windows-gnu (lib + bin) compiles; Linux tests pass.
- Extra commit f686978 (own): fixed the pre-existing Windows test-build error at group.rs:1984
  (`location: id * 1024` with id: u128 on Windows) so the PR's Windows test can be built.
- Runtime check of the Windows test under Wine: see entry below.

PR #299 (Patrick Wolf) - APPLIED as 64b4d23 (16 PR commits squashed into one commit authored by
Patrick Wolf; the squash is stated in the message) + correction 936f6bb (own).
- Read: new reflink_overwrite_dedupe() + fallback in linux_reflink + 7 tests. Flagged spots:
  (1) ioctl size, (2) handling of the per-destination status, (3) the bytes_deduped==0 break,
  (4) the test helper fideduperange_supported().
- Verified the flags:
  (1) C probe against linux/fs.h: FIDEDUPERANGE = 0xc0189436 (struct size 24); the PR encodes
      size 56 -> 0xc0389436 -> kernel returns ENOTTY on every filesystem -> the PR always falls
      back to the unchecked FICLONE. Its FIDEDUPERANGE tests printed "Skipping" and passed vacuously.
  (2) On this ZFS the correct ioctl returns 0 with status=-95 (EOPNOTSUPP), bytes_deduped=0: the
      PR would report that as success.
  (3) success with 0 bytes deduped -> loop break -> Ok: false success.
  (4) helper probes /tmp (overlayfs here) but tests run in target/test (ZFS), and every error
      other than ENOTTY/EOPNOTSUPP counted as "supported" -> after fixing (1) the 4 tests ran on
      ZFS and failed.
- Decision: apply. With the corrections it is never less safe than before (unsupported ->
  same FICLONE as before; supported -> kernel-verified dedupe), and it addresses #293/M12.
- Correction commit 936f6bb fixes (1)-(4) and adds two tests (request code == kernel value;
  unsupported FIDEDUPERANGE is an error). End-to-end on ZFS: `fclones dedupe` still dedupes
  (via FICLONE fallback), contents equal.
- NOT verifiable here: the FIDEDUPERANGE success path and the "contents differ" rejection need
  btrfs/XFS; only ZFS (FICLONE yes, FIDEDUPERANGE no) and tmpfs (neither) are available and the
  container has no mount capability. Those 4 tests skip with the correct reason now.
- Tests after task 4: 178 lib + 4 bin + 2 doc pass; cargo fmt clean.
- PR #365 runtime check under Wine (installed mingw-w64 + wine64 in the container):
  `cargo test --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu --lib path::` with #365: 9 pass / 2 fail
  (file_name, encode_decode_stfu8); the PR's new test non_utf8_file_name PASSES.
  Same command on the base commit (worktree at a74f90d + the test-build fix): 8 pass / the same
  2 fail -> both failures pre-exist on Windows (Path::file_name only special-cases "/" and not
  "\\" for roots, cf. review L-items) and are not caused by #365. => #365 verified.

