PR #339 + #340 + #341 (lovely90133; stacked) - NOT APPLIED.
- Read: replaces partition()'s per-file filtering with a whole-group validate_group() (regular
  file, size, mtime and - new, on by default - a full re-hash of every file compared with the
  group hash from the report); new SkipReason/GroupValidationResult/GroupProcessResult types,
  dedupe()/run_script()/log_script() signatures changed; #340 adds helper methods + tests; #341 adds
  a JSON dry-run whose format is silently taken from the *group* run's --format. Explanatory
  comments in partition()/log_script() deleted.
- Flagged and verified (built pr/341 in a separate worktree, compared with our build, each binary
  on its own reports):
  1. dedupe() splits link/dedupe groups by device and then `return`s after the FIRST partition:
     a group spanning ZFS + tmpfs produced 1 `ln` instead of 2 (3/3 runs) -> silently drops work.
  2. Hash validation assumes the report hash is a full-content hash of the raw file. It is not
     for --skip-content-hash (prefix^suffix), --transform (hash of the transformed output) or
     hard-link-only groups (hash 0). Verified: --skip-content-hash report of two identical 300 KB
     files -> "hash does not match", group skipped, 0 files processed (ours: 1).
  3. Re-reading every file fully before acting doubles the I/O of a dedupe run, enabled by default.
  4. Coupling of dry-run output format to the group command's --format (#341) is surprising.
- Decision: reject. The idea (re-validate before acting, issue #84) is good; I address the
  staleness part of #84 with a narrow ctime check in task 7 instead.

PR #335 (David Taylor) - NOT APPLIED.
- Read: new CollapseReflinks phase (Linux FIEMAP / macOS F_LOG2PHYS_EXT) that REMOVES files whose
  full extent map equals another file's from the size groups, unconditionally (no flag).
- Flagged: (1) default behavior change: reflinked copies disappear from reports, so `remove`/`move`
  users (who dedupe for tidiness, not space) no longer see those duplicates; (2) replica counting
  for --isolate / --rf-under / --unique changes: a file present in two roots as reflinks is counted
  once -> e.g. reported as under-replicated; (3) one FIEMAP ioctl + full extent list per candidate
  file on every run, also on SSDs where FetchExtents is skipped; (4) cannot be verified here: ZFS
  in this environment has FICLONE but no FIEMAP and btrfs/XFS are unavailable, so the new phase is a
  no-op on every filesystem I can test.
- Decision: reject as-is (unverifiable core + unflagged semantic change). Would be acceptable as
  an opt-in flag that only affects size statistics / skips already-shared groups for `dedupe`.

PR #317 (Koutheir Attouchi) - NOT APPLIED.
- Read per commit: dependency major bumps (bytesize 2, byte-unit 5, sysinfo 0.38, rand 0.10,
  nom 8, ...), edition 2024, MSRV 1.74 -> 1.89, lazy_static -> LazyLock, removal of unused deps,
