Task 7: remaining open issues (2026-11-16)
Fixed in this task (each with verification as described in its commit):
- #353 (link/dedupe fail with "File name too long") - FIXED e817f53. Temp name = <name>.<24
  random> only if it fits 255 bytes, else `.fclones-tmp.<random>` in the same dir. Test with
  250-char names fails with the old naming.
- #309 / #336 (RPM owns /usr/bin -> conflict with "filesystem" package) - FIXED 8694181.
  Verified on the released 0.35.0-2 RPM (`rpm -qlvp`: owns /usr, /usr/bin, /usr/share, ...).
  Root cause: alien 8.95 in the buster packaging image (fixed in alien 8.95.1, Debian #759533).
  First attempt (move the image to Debian trixie) was committed and then UNDONE before any push
  (git reset --soft): a binary built there needs GLIBC_2.39 instead of 2.28 and would not run on
  Rocky 9 (glibc 2.34), the very users of #309. Final fix: generate the spec with `alien -g`,
  delete %dir entries of system dirs, rpmbuild with a pinned output name format. Tested the script
  lines with the real cargo-deb package and injected buster-style %dir lines: RPM contains
  /usr/bin/fclones and owns only /usr/share/doc/fclones. Not tested: building the Docker image
  (no Docker here). An attempt to download and run buster's alien 8.95 to reproduce exactly was
  denied by the environment's permission policy; not worked around.
- #323 / #337 (startup triggers every automount, hangs on unreachable targets) - FIXED 247268b.
  sysinfo 0.29 statvfs()s every /proc/mounts entry incl. autofs; sysinfo 0.37 skips autofs but
  needs Rust 1.88 + API changes (= the kind of upgrade rejected with #317). On Linux the mount
  table is now read directly (sysinfo's filters + autofs, no statvfs), disk type from
  /sys/block/*/queue/rotational (ported from sysinfo 0.29, MIT). strace on this machine: 13
  statfs() calls at startup before, 0 after. Tests: filter with an autofs line; every disk
  sysinfo reports here appears with identical name/type/fs/removable flag. No autofs available
  here to test the hang itself.
- #298 (Windows Hidden attribute ignored) - FIXED f93eed8. FILE_ATTRIBUTE_HIDDEN checked when
  hidden files are excluded; Windows test via `attrib +h`, run under Wine (fails without the check).
  The crash in the same issue was fixed by PR #365.

